{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall nurse him for me.</b> Him alone, and not another with him. From here our Rabbis of blessed memory said: one who is hired to nurse the son of her fellow may not nurse another with him." "<b>And I shall give you your wage.</b> It is not enough for the righteous that their lost property is restored to them, but they are also given a wage. So too we find in Mordecai the righteous: it was not enough that he and his people were saved from slaughter, but they clothed him in royal garments of blue and white, and a great crown of gold."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:31.974717929Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}